add(POL,"L","legendary","legendary","Monetary tightening raises the domestic interest rate, while political risk simultaneously rises. What can be concluded about the currency?","Its direction is ambiguous because lower NCO from returns opposes higher NCO from risk",["It appreciates because the policy-rate channel is transmitted before portfolios rebalance","It depreciates because political risk shifts currency demand rather than supply","It is unchanged because monetary policy affects the nominal rate while risk affects the real rate"],"Higher returns tend to reduce currency supply and appreciate the currency; higher risk tends to raise supply and depreciate it.","analyze_competing_policy_channels");
